  "rationale": "The workflow runs Composer install on every matrix job with no dependency cache, so dependencies are refetched on each run. The P-LIT-GHA-CACHE pattern (Cache dependency downloads) supports caching dependency downloads keyed on the lockfile, with reported modest aggregate VM-time savings, and the measured experiment example (experiment:batch-hiruni-pattern-bat-ae496965ffa682a2-r2) showed dependency caching reduced elapsed CI time. Adding a Composer cache step before composer install preserves all existing build and test coverage, keeps permissions unchanged (contents: read), adds no secrets, privileged actions, publishing/deployment, or new network access beyond the existing composer install, and invalidates automatically when composer.lock changes.",
